01:23:56,000 --> 01:24:02,159
First order logic is weak enough that

1969
01:23:58,159 --> 01:24:04,239
its truths coincide with its theorems.

1970
01:24:02,159 --> 01:24:09,040
Arithmetic and set theory are rich

1971
01:24:04,239 --> 01:24:10,800
enough that truth exceeds provability.

1972
01:24:09,040 --> 01:24:13,360
Girdle's completeness theorem had

1973
01:24:10,800 --> 01:24:15,600
important consequences.

1974
01:24:13,360 --> 01:24:19,920
It showed that model theory and proof

1975
01:24:15,600 --> 01:24:22,560
theory are two sides of the same coin.

1976
01:24:19,920 --> 01:24:26,320
A statement is provable if and only if

1977
01:24:22,560 --> 01:24:28,480
it is true in all models.

1978
01:24:26,320 --> 01:24:30,639
This duality became fundamental to

1979
01:24:28,480 --> 01:24:33,199
modern logic.

1980
01:24:30,639 --> 01:24:36,719
It also showed that consistency and

1981
01:24:33,199 --> 01:24:39,760
satisfiability are equivalent. A theory

1982
01:24:36,719 --> 01:24:42,080
is consistent if and only if it has a

1983
01:24:39,760 --> 01:24:44,000
model.

1984
01:24:42,080 --> 01:24:45,760
But there is a philosophical puzzle

1985
01:24:44,000 --> 01:24:48,480
here.

1986
01:24:45,760 --> 01:24:51,760
Completeness seems to suggest that logic

1987
01:24:48,480 --> 01:24:54,960
fully captures logical truth.

1988
01:24:51,760 --> 01:24:56,560
Everything valid is provable.

1989
01:24:54,960 --> 01:24:59,120
Yet incompleteness shows that

1990
01:24:56,560 --> 01:25:01,760
mathematics cannot be fully captured by

1991
01:24:59,120 --> 01:25:04,880
any axiom system.

1992
01:25:01,760 --> 01:25:07,120
How do these fit together?

1993
01:25:04,880 --> 01:25:09,840
The answer is that logic and mathematics

1994
01:25:07,120 --> 01:25:12,719
have different structures.

1995
01:25:09,840 --> 01:25:15,679
Logic deals with the form of arguments

1996
01:25:12,719 --> 01:25:18,080
independent of content.

1997
01:25:15,679 --> 01:25:20,880
Any statement expressible purely in

1998
01:25:18,080 --> 01:25:23,760
logical vocabulary using only

1999
01:25:20,880 --> 01:25:25,280
quantifiers, connectives, identity and

2000
01:25:23,760 --> 01:25:29,040
variables

2001
01:25:25,280 --> 01:25:31,760
is decided by logical rules.

2002
01:25:29,040 --> 01:25:34,480
But mathematics introduces content

2003
01:25:31,760 --> 01:25:38,719
through non-logical concepts like

2004
01:25:34,480 --> 01:25:40,880
number, set, function.

2005
01:25:38,719 --> 01:25:43,120
These concepts have richness that

2006
01:25:40,880 --> 01:25:45,440
exceeds what first order logic can

2007
01:25:43,120 --> 01:25:47,920
formalize.

2008
01:25:45,440 --> 01:25:52,239
Once you add mathematical axioms to

2009
01:25:47,920 --> 01:25:54,400
logic, you get incompleteness.

2010
01:25:52,239 --> 01:25:56,639
Girdle saw this as revealing something

2011
01:25:54,400 --> 01:25:58,560
deep about the nature of mathematical

2012
01:25:56,639 --> 01:26:01,840
concepts.

2013
01:25:58,560 --> 01:26:05,040
They are not reducible to logic.

2014
01:26:01,840 --> 01:26:07,199
The concept of number for instance has a

2015
01:26:05,040 --> 01:26:10,719
content that goes beyond anything

2016
01:26:07,199 --> 01:26:12,880
expressible in pure logic.

2017
01:26:10,719 --> 01:26:16,880
This is why mathematics needs its own

2018
01:26:12,880 --> 01:26:19,520
axioms beyond logical axioms and why

2019
01:26:16,880 --> 01:26:23,120
those mathematical axioms inevitably

2020
01:26:19,520 --> 01:26:25,520
leave some truths unprovable.

2021
01:26:23,120 --> 01:26:28,639
This anti-logicist message connected to

2022
01:26:25,520 --> 01:26:30,480
Girdle's criticism of Fraga and Russell.

2023
01:26:28,639 --> 01:26:32,719
They tried to reduce mathematics to

2024
01:26:30,480 --> 01:26:35,760
logic, showing that mathematical truths

2025
01:26:32,719 --> 01:26:37,920
are just complex logical truths.

2026
01:26:35,760 --> 01:26:40,239
Girdle's completeness and incompleteness

2027
01:26:37,920 --> 01:26:43,199
theorems together undermined this

2028
01:26:40,239 --> 01:26:45,600
program. Logic is complete, but

2029
01:26:43,199 --> 01:26:48,159
mathematics is not. Therefore,

2030
01:26:45,600 --> 01:26:50,320
mathematics cannot be reduced to logic.

2031
01:26:48,159 --> 01:26:52,960
It has its own irreducible subject

2032
01:26:50,320 --> 01:26:55,040
matter. The completeness theorem also

2033
01:26:52,960 --> 01:26:57,679
had technical applications that Girdle

2034
01:26:55,040 --> 01:27:00,159
explored. It implies the compactness

2035
01:26:57,679 --> 01:27:03,040
theorem which says that if every finite

2036
01:27:00,159 --> 01:27:06,400
subset of a set of axioms has a model

2037
01:27:03,040 --> 01:27:08,000
then the whole infinite set has a model.

2038
01:27:06,400 --> 01:27:10,719
This leads to the existence of

2039
01:27:08,000 --> 01:27:13,199
non-standard models structures

2040
01:27:10,719 --> 01:27:14,480
satisfying the axioms but looking very

2041
01:27:13,199 --> 01:27:16,400
different from the intended

2042
01:27:14,480 --> 01:27:18,800
interpretation.

2043
01:27:16,400 --> 01:27:20,719
For arithmetic, compactness implies

2044
01:27:18,800 --> 01:27:23,840
there are models with infinite numbers

2045
01:27:20,719 --> 01:27:26,080
beyond all standard natural numbers.

2046
01:27:23,840 --> 01:27:28,960
These non-standard models satisfy all

2047
01:27:26,080 --> 01:27:31,199
the axioms of arithmetic but contain

2048
01:27:28,960 --> 01:27:33,520
bizarre elements.

2049
01:27:31,199 --> 01:27:35,199
For set theory, there are models with

2050
01:27:33,520 --> 01:27:37,600
different cardalities and different

2051
01:27:35,199 --> 01:27:40,400
hierarchies of infinities.

2052
01:27:37,600 --> 01:27:42,960
All satisfy the axioms, but they differ

2053
01:27:40,400 --> 01:27:45,120
radically in structure.

2054
01:27:42,960 --> 01:27:47,520
Does this mean arithmetic and set theory

2055
01:27:45,120 --> 01:27:50,159
are ambiguous with no determinant

2056
01:27:47,520 --> 01:27:53,120
intended interpretation?

2057
01:27:50,159 --> 01:27:55,600
Some philosophers have argued yes. The

2058
01:27:53,120 --> 01:27:58,000
axioms do not uniquely fix what we are

2059
01:27:55,600 --> 01:28:00,560
talking about. So there is no fact about

2060
01:27:58,000 --> 01:28:02,800
which model is correct.

2061
01:28:00,560 --> 01:28:04,719
Mathematical truth is relative to a

2062
01:28:02,800 --> 01:28:07,679
choice of model.

2063
01:28:04,719 --> 01:28:09,760
Girdle rejected this forcefully. He

2064
01:28:07,679 --> 01:28:12,400
insisted that we intend to talk about

2065
01:28:09,760 --> 01:28:14,560
the standard natural numbers or the full

2066
01:28:12,400 --> 01:28:16,639
universe of sets.

2067
01:28:14,560 --> 01:28:19,120
Our axioms may fail to capture this

2068
01:28:16,639 --> 01:28:21,280
intention fully, but the intention is

2069
01:28:19,120 --> 01:28:23,600
there nonetheless.

2070
01:28:21,280 --> 01:28:26,320
Non-standard models are artifacts of the

2071
01:28:23,600 --> 01:28:28,480
weakness of first order logic, not

2072
01:28:26,320 --> 01:28:30,880
evidence against objective mathematical

2073
01:28:28,480 --> 01:28:32,719
truth. This connects back to his

2074
01:28:30,880 --> 01:28:34,719
Platonism.

2075
01:28:32,719 --> 01:28:37,679
Mathematical concepts are grasped

2076
01:28:34,719 --> 01:28:40,880
intuitively and this intuition fixes a

2077
01:28:37,679 --> 01:28:44,159
unique intended interpretation even when

2078
01:28:40,880 --> 01:28:46,159
formal axioms underdetermine it. The

2079
01:28:44,159 --> 01:28:48,800
axioms are attempts to describe the

2080
01:28:46,159 --> 01:28:51,679
concepts and we revise axioms when they

2081
01:28:48,800 --> 01:28:53,840
fail to capture what we intend. But the

2082
01:28:51,679 --> 01:28:56,880
concepts themselves and the structures

2083
01:28:53,840 --> 01:28:58,800
they pick out are objective. Let me

2084
01:28:56,880 --> 01:29:01,760
conclude this part by reflecting on

2085
01:28:58,800 --> 01:29:04,400
Girdle's legacy in set theory.

2086
01:29:01,760 --> 01:29:07,360
His work on constructibility, the

2087
01:29:04,400 --> 01:29:10,320
continuum hypothesis and large cardinals

2088
01:29:07,360 --> 01:29:13,280
reshaped the field. The techniques he

2089
01:29:10,320 --> 01:29:16,320
developed, inner models, consistency

2090
01:29:13,280 --> 01:29:18,800
proofs, relative consistency

2091
01:29:16,320 --> 01:29:20,960
became standard tools.

2092
01:29:18,800 --> 01:29:23,760
His philosophical vision of seeking new

2093
01:29:20,960 --> 01:29:27,040
axioms to settle independent questions

2094
01:29:23,760 --> 01:29:28,880
guides contemporary research.

2095
01:29:27,040 --> 01:29:30,719
Yet the problems he cared most about

2096
01:29:28,880 --> 01:29:32,880
remain unsolved.

2097
01:29:30,719 --> 01:29:35,040
The continuum hypothesis is still

2098
01:29:32,880 --> 01:29:36,960
independent of standard axioms plus

2099
01:29:35,040 --> 01:29:39,440
large cardinals.

2100
01:29:36,960 --> 01:29:41,920
No consensus exists on what axioms

2101
01:29:39,440 --> 01:29:43,840
should extend ZF.

2102
01:29:41,920 --> 01:29:45,760
The philosophical questions about

2103
01:29:43,840 --> 01:29:49,840
mathematical truth and the nature of

2104
01:29:45,760 --> 01:29:52,880
sets are as contested as ever. Some see

2105
01:29:49,840 --> 01:29:55,760
this as failure. Girdle's program has

2106
01:29:52,880 --> 01:29:58,080
not delivered what he hoped.

2107
01:29:55,760 --> 01:30:00,000
Others see it as evidence of the depth

2108
01:29:58,080 --> 01:30:01,600
and difficulty of the questions he

2109
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:03,840
raised.

2110
01:30:01,600 --> 01:30:07,120
Set theory after Girdle has become a

2111
01:30:03,840 --> 01:30:09,360
rich sophisticated field exploring the

2112
01:30:07,120 --> 01:30:12,080
upper reaches of infinity and the

2113
01:30:09,360 --> 01:30:13,840
foundations of mathematics.

2114
01:30:12,080 --> 01:30:16,080
His incompleteness theorems and

2115
01:30:13,840 --> 01:30:19,040
constructibility results showed that

2116
01:30:16,080 --> 01:30:21,440
simple answers were impossible, forcing

2117
01:30:19,040 --> 01:30:23,520
mathematicians to develop new tools and

2118
01:30:21,440 --> 01:30:25,840
ideas.

2119
01:30:23,520 --> 01:30:28,960
Perhaps the deepest lesson is that

2120
01:30:25,840 --> 01:30:31,920
mathematics is inexhaustible.

2121
01:30:28,960 --> 01:30:35,199
No matter how far we extend our axioms,

2122
01:30:31,920 --> 01:30:37,520
independent questions will remain. The

2123
01:30:35,199 --> 01:30:40,639
structure of mathematical reality is so

2124
01:30:37,520 --> 01:30:43,040
rich that no finite axiomatization can

2125
01:30:40,639 --> 01:30:46,159
capture it completely.

2126
01:30:43,040 --> 01:30:49,520
This is not a defect but a reflection of

2127
01:30:46,159 --> 01:30:52,080
the infinite depth of mathematics.

2128
01:30:49,520 --> 01:30:54,560
Girdle revealed this depth and his work

2129
01:30:52,080 --> 01:30:56,400
remains a foundation for anyone

2130
01:30:54,560 --> 01:31:00,199
exploring the ultimate nature of

2131
01:30:56,400 --> 01:31:00,199
mathematical truth.

2132
01:31:01,520 --> 01:31:07,440
Part four, logic and completeness.

2133
01:31:05,840 --> 01:31:09,120
Before Kurt Girdle shattered

2134
01:31:07,440 --> 01:31:11,600
mathematical certainty within

2135
01:31:09,120 --> 01:31:14,400
completeness, he established something

2136
01:31:11,600 --> 01:31:16,639
equally profound, the completeness of

2137
01:31:14,400 --> 01:31:18,800
first order logic.

2138
01:31:16,639 --> 01:31:20,320
This was his doctoral dissertation in

2139
01:31:18,800 --> 01:31:24,320
1929,

2140
01:31:20,320 --> 01:31:26,080
submitted when he was just 23 years old.

2141
01:31:24,320 --> 01:31:28,400
The completeness theorem proved that

2142
01:31:26,080 --> 01:31:30,960
logical truth and provability coincide

2143
01:31:28,400 --> 01:31:33,120
in first order logic.

2144
01:31:30,960 --> 01:31:35,600
Every statement that is logically valid

2145
01:31:33,120 --> 01:31:38,800
can be formally proven.

2146
01:31:35,600 --> 01:31:40,320
Logic at least is complete.

2147
01:31:38,800 --> 01:31:42,400
This achievement alone would have

2148
01:31:40,320 --> 01:31:45,440
secured Girdle's place in the history of

2149
01:31:42,400 --> 01:31:47,360
logic. But the completeness theorem is

2150
01:31:45,440 --> 01:31:48,560
also where Girdle first developed the

2151
01:31:47,360 --> 01:31:50,960
techniques that would lead to

2152
01:31:48,560 --> 01:31:53,360
incompleteness.

2153
01:31:50,960 --> 01:31:55,920
Understanding what he proved, why it

2154
01:31:53,360 --> 01:31:58,960
matters, and how it relates to his later

2155
01:31:55,920 --> 01:32:02,600
work reveals the profound unity of his

2156
01:31:58,960 --> 01:32:02,600
logical investigations.

2157
01:32:02,880 --> 01:32:07,199
The problem Goodel addressed concerned

2158
01:32:04,960 --> 01:32:10,480
the relationship between semantics and

2159
01:32:07,199 --> 01:32:13,280
syntax in logic. Semantics deals with

2160
01:32:10,480 --> 01:32:15,520
meaning and truth. When is a logical

2161
01:32:13,280 --> 01:32:18,719
formula true?

2162
01:32:15,520 --> 01:32:21,600
Syntax deals with formal proof. When can

2163
01:32:18,719 --> 01:32:24,080
a formula be derived from axioms using

2164
01:32:21,600 --> 01:32:26,880
rules of inference?

2165
01:32:24,080 --> 01:32:29,440
David Hilbert and Wilhelm Acriman had

2166
01:32:26,880 --> 01:32:32,639
formulated a system of axioms and rules

2167
01:32:29,440 --> 01:32:34,800
for first order logic in 1928

2168
01:32:32,639 --> 01:32:37,760
and they asked whether this system was

2169
01:32:34,800 --> 01:32:40,000
complete, whether every valid formula

2170
01:32:37,760 --> 01:32:42,159
could be proven.

2171
01:32:40,000 --> 01:32:45,120
First order logic is the logic of

2172
01:32:42,159 --> 01:32:48,960
quantifiers and predicates. It allows

2173
01:32:45,120 --> 01:32:53,199
statements like for all X if X is human

2174
01:32:48,960 --> 01:32:55,760
then X is mortal or there exist an X

2175
01:32:53,199 --> 01:32:59,920
such that X is prime and X is greater

2176
01:32:55,760 --> 01:33:03,360
than 2. These statements use quantifiers

2177
01:32:59,920 --> 01:33:06,400
for all there exists ranging over a

2178
01:33:03,360 --> 01:33:10,560
domain of objects plus predicates

2179
01:33:06,400 --> 01:33:13,280
expressing properties of those objects.

2180
01:33:10,560 --> 01:33:16,719
A formula is logically valid if it is

2181
01:33:13,280 --> 01:33:20,560
true in all possible interpretations.

2182
01:33:16,719 --> 01:33:24,639
For instance, the formula for all x

2183
01:33:20,560 --> 01:33:26,480
either p of x or not p of x is valid

2184
01:33:24,639 --> 01:33:29,520
because no matter what domain you

2185
01:33:26,480 --> 01:33:33,280
consider and no matter what property p

2186
01:33:29,520 --> 01:33:36,320
represents, the statement is true. Every

2187
01:33:33,280 --> 01:33:39,520
object either has property p or lacks

2188
01:33:36,320 --> 01:33:42,000
it. This is the law of excluded middle

2189
01:33:39,520 --> 01:33:44,880
applied to predicates.

2190
01:33:42,000 --> 01:33:47,679
A formula is provable if it can be

2191
01:33:44,880 --> 01:33:49,600
derived from logical axioms using rules

2192
01:33:47,679 --> 01:33:52,560
of inference.

2193
01:33:49,600 --> 01:33:55,840
Start with basic logical truths like A

2194
01:33:52,560 --> 01:33:59,440
implies A and apply rules like modus

2195
01:33:55,840 --> 01:34:03,600
ponins. If you have proved A and proved

2196
01:33:59,440 --> 01:34:06,239
A implies B, you can derive B.

2197
01:34:03,600 --> 01:34:09,760
To generate new theorems, the question

2198
01:34:06,239 --> 01:34:13,120
is whether these two notions coincide.

2199
01:34:09,760 --> 01:34:16,159
Is every valid formula provable?

2200
01:34:13,120 --> 01:34:19,440
This is what completeness asks.

2201
01:34:16,159 --> 01:34:21,760
Goodel proved the answer is yes. He

2202
01:34:19,440 --> 01:34:24,000
showed that the Hilbert Acriman axiom

2203
01:34:21,760 --> 01:34:25,520
system for first order logic is

2204
01:34:24,000 --> 01:34:27,760
complete.

2205
01:34:25,520 --> 01:34:29,600
Every logically valid formula is

2206
01:34:27,760 --> 01:34:32,320
provable.

2207
01:34:29,600 --> 01:34:35,360
The proof was ingenious and involved

2208
01:34:32,320 --> 01:34:37,600
constructing for any unprovable formula

2209
01:34:35,360 --> 01:34:39,199
an interpretation where the formula is

2210
01:34:37,600 --> 01:34:41,600
false.

2211
01:34:39,199 --> 01:34:44,639
This showed that unprovable formulas are

2212
01:34:41,600 --> 01:34:47,600
not valid. Hence, provable formulas

2213
01:34:44,639 --> 01:34:50,560
coincide with valid ones.

2214
01:34:47,600 --> 01:34:53,440
The technique God used anticipated later

2215
01:34:50,560 --> 01:34:55,360
model theoretic methods. He showed how

2216
01:34:53,440 --> 01:34:56,880
to build models of logical theories

2217
01:34:55,360 --> 01:34:58,960
systematically,

2218
01:34:56,880 --> 01:35:00,560
checking whether formulas hold in those

2219
01:34:58,960 --> 01:35:02,960
models.

2220
01:35:00,560 --> 01:35:04,880
This gave birth to model theory as a

2221
01:35:02,960 --> 01:35:06,960
branch of logic.

2222
01:35:04,880 --> 01:35:09,600
The interplay between syntax and

2223
01:35:06,960 --> 01:35:12,639
semantics became a central theme in 20th

2224
01:35:09,600 --> 01:35:15,280
century logic largely due to God's

2225
01:35:12,639 --> 01:35:18,320
completeness theorem.

2226
01:35:15,280 --> 01:35:20,320
But why does completeness matter? What

2227
01:35:18,320 --> 01:35:22,320
hangs on whether valid formulas are

2228
01:35:20,320 --> 01:35:24,960
provable?

2229
01:35:22,320 --> 01:35:27,280
First, completeness establishes that

2230
01:35:24,960 --> 01:35:30,000
formal proof systems capture all of

2231
01:35:27,280 --> 01:35:32,560
logical truth. If you want to know

2232
01:35:30,000 --> 01:35:35,520
whether a statement is logically valid,

2233
01:35:32,560 --> 01:35:38,239
you can try to find a proof. If it is

2234
01:35:35,520 --> 01:35:40,480
valid, a proof exists.

2235
01:35:38,239 --> 01:35:42,639
This vindicates the idea that logical

2236
01:35:40,480 --> 01:35:45,760
reasoning can be formalized without

2237
01:35:42,639 --> 01:35:48,320
losing anything essential.

2238
01:35:45,760 --> 01:35:51,679
Everything inferable by pure logic can

2239
01:35:48,320 --> 01:35:54,080
be inferred by mechanical rules.

2240
01:35:51,679 --> 01:35:56,480
Second, completeness implies that

2241
01:35:54,080 --> 01:35:58,000
consistency and satisfiability are

2242
01:35:56,480 --> 01:36:01,120
equivalent.

2243
01:35:58,000 --> 01:36:03,520
A set of axioms is consistent. It does

2244
01:36:01,120 --> 01:36:05,920
not prove contradictions

2245
01:36:03,520 --> 01:36:09,040
if and only if those axioms have a

