2308
01:38:49,119 --> 01:38:54,880
Completeness or categoricity,

2309
01:38:51,920 --> 01:38:57,280
but not both. Good's philosophical

2310
01:38:54,880 --> 01:38:59,520
interpretation was that mathematical

2311
01:38:57,280 --> 01:39:02,560
concepts have a richness that exceeds

2312
01:38:59,520 --> 01:39:04,400
any fixed logical formalism.

2313
01:39:02,560 --> 01:39:07,920
The concept of natural number for

2314
01:39:04,400 --> 01:39:10,960
instance determines a unique structure

2315
01:39:07,920 --> 01:39:13,119
the standard natural numbers. But no

2316
01:39:10,960 --> 01:39:15,280
first order axioms can pin down this

2317
01:39:13,119 --> 01:39:18,320
structure uniquely.

2318
01:39:15,280 --> 01:39:20,400
We need second order axioms but then we

2319
01:39:18,320 --> 01:39:22,000
