Think of it this way. Imagine spacetime

2803
01:59:46,080 --> 01:59:51,440
as a fabric that can be twisted.

2804
01:59:49,119 --> 01:59:53,040
In flat spacetime, no amount of

2805
01:59:51,440 --> 01:59:54,639
traveling brings you back to your own

2806
01:59:53,040 --> 01:59:56,880
past.

2807
01:59:54,639 --> 01:59:58,880
But in Good's universe, the rotation

2808
01:59:56,880 --> 02:00:01,360
twists the fabric of spacetime so

2809
01:59:58,880 --> 02:00:03,920
severely that the future direction

2810
02:00:01,360 --> 02:00:05,599
eventually curves back to meet the past.

2811
02:00:03,920 --> 02:00:08,400
Following a straight path through this

2812
02:00:05,599 --> 02:00:10,639
twisted spacetime, you loop back to your

2813
02:00:08,400 --> 02:00:12,719
starting point.

2814
02:00:10,639 --> 02:00:15,599
The philosophical implications hit

2815
02:00:12,719 --> 02:00:17,840
Einstein hard. He had spent decades

2816
02:00:15,599 --> 02:00:21,119
convinced that time is relative, but

2817
02:00:17,840 --> 02:00:23,599
that causality is absolute. Events have

2818
02:00:21,119 --> 02:00:26,320
a definite order. Causes proceed

2819
02:00:23,599 --> 02:00:29,360
effects. The possibility of closed

2820
02:00:26,320 --> 02:00:31,920
timelike curves threaten this. If you

2821
02:00:29,360 --> 02:00:35,199
can travel to your own past, paradoxes

2822
02:00:31,920 --> 02:00:37,119
arise. You could prevent your own birth,

2823
02:00:35,199 --> 02:00:39,360
kill your grandfather before your parent

2824
02:00:37,119 --> 02:00:41,840
was born, or create logical

2825
02:00:39,360 --> 02:00:43,760
contradictions.

2826
02:00:41,840 --> 02:00:46,639
Goodell was aware of these paradoxes,

2827
02:00:43,760 --> 02:00:49,040
but not troubled by them. He saw closed

2828
02:00:46,639 --> 02:00:51,840
timelike curves as evidence that time is

2829
02:00:49,040 --> 02:00:53,760
not what we ordinarily think.

2830
02:00:51,840 --> 02:00:56,239
The intuitive concept of time as a

2831
02:00:53,760 --> 02:00:58,719
one-way flow from past through present

2832
02:00:56,239 --> 02:01:00,800
to future does not correspond to

2833
02:00:58,719 --> 02:01:02,480
anything in the objective structure of

2834
02:01:00,800 --> 02:01:05,679
spaceime.

2835
02:01:02,480 --> 02:01:07,840
Time in this sense is ideal, not a

2836
02:01:05,679 --> 02:01:11,520
feature of reality itself, but a

2837
02:01:07,840 --> 02:01:13,679
subjective phenomenon of consciousness.

2838
02:01:11,520 --> 02:01:16,080
This conclusion connected to Goodell's

2839
02:01:13,679 --> 02:01:18,320
engagement with contean and idealist

2840
02:01:16,080 --> 02:01:20,080
philosophy, which I will explore in the

2841
02:01:18,320 --> 02:01:22,239
next part.

2842
02:01:20,080 --> 02:01:24,480
For now, note that Goodell's argument

2843
02:01:22,239 --> 02:01:26,239
was not just that time travel produces

2844
02:01:24,480 --> 02:01:28,239
paradoxes.

2845
02:01:26,239 --> 02:01:30,639
Rather, he argued that the very

2846
02:01:28,239 --> 02:01:33,360
existence of closed timelike curves in a

2847
02:01:30,639 --> 02:01:36,080
solution to Einstein's equations shows

2848
02:01:33,360 --> 02:01:39,119
that time as ordinarily conceived does

2849
02:01:36,080 --> 02:01:41,840
not exist in the physical world.

2850
02:01:39,119 --> 02:01:44,320
His reasoning went like this.

2851
02:01:41,840 --> 02:01:47,040
If Einstein's equations allow universes

2852
02:01:44,320 --> 02:01:48,960
with closed timelike curves and if those

2853
02:01:47,040 --> 02:01:51,280
equations correctly describe the

2854
02:01:48,960 --> 02:01:53,679
structure of spaceime, then the

2855
02:01:51,280 --> 02:01:55,679
possibility of such universes reveals

2856
02:01:53,679 --> 02:01:59,599
something about the nature of time in

2857
02:01:55,679 --> 02:02:01,840
all universes, including ours.

2858
02:01:59,599 --> 02:02:05,520
Specifically, it shows that there is no

2859
02:02:01,840 --> 02:02:07,920
objective global time, no way to divide

2860
02:02:05,520 --> 02:02:11,119
spaceime into a sequence of now moments

2861
02:02:07,920 --> 02:02:13,440
that all observers would agree on.

2862
02:02:11,119 --> 02:02:16,000
In ordinary relativistic spacetimes

2863
02:02:13,440 --> 02:02:18,000
without closed curves, you can define a

2864
02:02:16,000 --> 02:02:22,000
global time function that increases

2865
02:02:18,000 --> 02:02:24,320
monotonically along all timelike paths.

2866
02:02:22,000 --> 02:02:26,639
Events can be ordered as earlier and

2867
02:02:24,320 --> 02:02:28,880
later in a way consistent across the

2868
02:02:26,639 --> 02:02:30,960
entire universe.

2869
02:02:28,880 --> 02:02:34,080
But in Goodell's universe, no such

2870
02:02:30,960 --> 02:02:36,719
function exists. Time is local and

2871
02:02:34,080 --> 02:02:40,239
relative to a degree that destroys any

2872
02:02:36,719 --> 02:02:42,960
objective temporal order.

2873
02:02:40,239 --> 02:02:44,719
Critics objected immediately.

2874
02:02:42,960 --> 02:02:47,280
Our universe does not rotate like

2875
02:02:44,719 --> 02:02:49,360
Goodell's universe. Astronomical

2876
02:02:47,280 --> 02:02:52,080
observations show no large-scale

2877
02:02:49,360 --> 02:02:54,880
rotation. So Goodell's solution is

2878
02:02:52,080 --> 02:02:56,960
physically irrelevant. A mathematical

2879
02:02:54,880 --> 02:03:01,199
curiosity allowed by Einstein's

2880
02:02:56,960 --> 02:03:03,440
equations, but not realized in nature.

2881
02:03:01,199 --> 02:03:05,199
Goodell anticipated this objection and

2882
02:03:03,440 --> 02:03:07,520
had a reply.

2883
02:03:05,199 --> 02:03:10,320
The argument is not that our universe is

2884
02:03:07,520 --> 02:03:12,960
a Goodell universe. It is that the

2885
02:03:10,320 --> 02:03:16,080
physical laws describing our universe,

2886
02:03:12,960 --> 02:03:17,840
Einstein's equations, permit Gdell

2887
02:03:16,080 --> 02:03:20,080
universes.

2888
02:03:17,840 --> 02:03:22,639
This possibility reveals something about

2889
02:03:20,080 --> 02:03:26,880
the laws themselves and therefore about

2890
02:03:22,639 --> 02:03:28,960
all universes governed by those laws.

2891
02:03:26,880 --> 02:03:31,199
Think of an analogy.

2892
02:03:28,960 --> 02:03:34,400
Newtonian mechanics allows frictionless

2893
02:03:31,199 --> 02:03:37,520
planes and perfectly elastic collisions,

2894
02:03:34,400 --> 02:03:39,599
neither of which exists in nature.

2895
02:03:37,520 --> 02:03:42,080
But studying these idealized cases

2896
02:03:39,599 --> 02:03:45,040
reveals features of Newtonian mechanics

2897
02:03:42,080 --> 02:03:47,520
relevant to actual systems.

2898
02:03:45,040 --> 02:03:49,599
Similarly, studying Goodell's rotating

2899
02:03:47,520 --> 02:03:51,679
universe reveals features of general

2900
02:03:49,599 --> 02:03:56,239
relativity relevant to understanding

2901
02:03:51,679 --> 02:03:58,159
time in any relativistic universe.

2902
02:03:56,239 --> 02:04:00,159
The feature Goodell thought he had

2903
02:03:58,159 --> 02:04:02,639
revealed is that general relativity

2904
02:04:00,159 --> 02:04:04,639
provides no support for an objective

2905
02:04:02,639 --> 02:04:06,400
flow of time.

2906
02:04:04,639 --> 02:04:08,719
The theory describes space-time

2907
02:04:06,400 --> 02:04:11,440
structure but does not privilege any

2908
02:04:08,719 --> 02:04:13,040
particular notion of past, present and

2909
02:04:11,440 --> 02:04:15,199
future.

2910
02:04:13,040 --> 02:04:18,400
Time is not built into the fabric of

2911
02:04:15,199 --> 02:04:20,800
reality according to general relativity.

2912
02:04:18,400 --> 02:04:24,880
It emerges from our perspective as

2913
02:04:20,800 --> 02:04:26,480
observers moving through spacetime.

2914
02:04:24,880 --> 02:04:28,080
This interpretation remains

2915
02:04:26,480 --> 02:04:30,239
controversial.

2916
02:04:28,080 --> 02:04:32,400
Many physicists and philosophers think

2917
02:04:30,239 --> 02:04:34,320
Goodell overreached.

2918
02:04:32,400 --> 02:04:36,400
Just because a theory allows bizarre

2919
02:04:34,320 --> 02:04:39,679
solutions does not mean those solutions

2920
02:04:36,400 --> 02:04:42,239
tell us about the actual world.

2921
02:04:39,679 --> 02:04:45,040
General relativity also allows wormholes

2922
02:04:42,239 --> 02:04:47,040
and naked singularities. But we do not

2923
02:04:45,040 --> 02:04:49,280
conclude that spacetime is therefore

2924
02:04:47,040 --> 02:04:52,719
riddled with wormholes where that

2925
02:04:49,280 --> 02:04:54,960
singularities are visible.

2926
02:04:52,719 --> 02:04:57,520
Moreover, subsequent work has shown that

2927
02:04:54,960 --> 02:05:00,639
not all rotating universes have closed

2928
02:04:57,520 --> 02:05:04,000
timelike curves. Some models exhibit

2929
02:05:00,639 --> 02:05:06,000
rotation without allowing time travel.

2930
02:05:04,000 --> 02:05:09,040
This weakens Goodell's claim that

2931
02:05:06,000 --> 02:05:11,920
rotation plus general relativity implies

2932
02:05:09,040 --> 02:05:14,320
temporal ideality.

2933
02:05:11,920 --> 02:05:16,400
Yet, Goodell's work stimulated immense

2934
02:05:14,320 --> 02:05:18,159
interest in the causal structure of

2935
02:05:16,400 --> 02:05:20,880
spaceime.

2936
02:05:18,159 --> 02:05:23,360
Physicists began systematically studying

2937
02:05:20,880 --> 02:05:25,760
which space-time geometries allow closed

2938
02:05:23,360 --> 02:05:28,080
timelike curves, under what conditions

2939
02:05:25,760 --> 02:05:31,040
they arise, and whether they can be

2940
02:05:28,080 --> 02:05:33,760
created artificially.

2941
02:05:31,040 --> 02:05:36,960
This led to investigations of chronology

2942
02:05:33,760 --> 02:05:38,880
protection, hypothetical mechanisms that

2943
02:05:36,960 --> 02:05:40,719
prevent closed timelike curves from

2944
02:05:38,880 --> 02:05:43,199
forming.

2945
02:05:40,719 --> 02:05:45,280
Stephven Hawking proposed a chronology

2946
02:05:43,199 --> 02:05:47,520
protection conjecture.

2947
02:05:45,280 --> 02:05:50,159
The laws of physics prevent time travel

2948
02:05:47,520 --> 02:05:52,000
to the past. Whenever conditions

2949
02:05:50,159 --> 02:05:54,400
approach those needed for closed

2950
02:05:52,000 --> 02:05:57,119
timelike curves, quantum effects

2951
02:05:54,400 --> 02:06:00,880
intervene to prevent them. This remains

2952
02:05:57,119 --> 02:06:02,800
unproven, and some physicists doubt it.

2953
02:06:00,880 --> 02:06:05,119
But the debate stems directly from

2954
02:06:02,800 --> 02:06:08,400
Goodell's discovery that classical

2955
02:06:05,119 --> 02:06:11,360
general relativity allows time travel.

2956
02:06:08,400 --> 02:06:13,920
Another legacy of Goodell's cosmological

2957
02:06:11,360 --> 02:06:16,719
work is the realization that the global

2958
02:06:13,920 --> 02:06:19,119
structure of spaceime matters.

2959
02:06:16,719 --> 02:06:22,880
Early work in relativity focused on

2960
02:06:19,119 --> 02:06:25,360
local properties, curvature at a point,

2961
02:06:22,880 --> 02:06:27,280
trajectories of particles, field

2962
02:06:25,360 --> 02:06:30,560
equations.

2963
02:06:27,280 --> 02:06:33,040
Goodell showed that global topology, how

2964
02:06:30,560 --> 02:06:36,800
spacetime connects to itself over large

2965
02:06:33,040 --> 02:06:39,119
scales, has physical significance.

2966
02:06:36,800 --> 02:06:41,840
This global perspective became central

2967
02:06:39,119 --> 02:06:44,480
to modern cosmology and the study of

2968
02:06:41,840 --> 02:06:46,480
black holes.

2969
02:06:44,480 --> 02:06:50,079
Let me describe the technical features

2970
02:06:46,480 --> 02:06:52,639
of Goodell's universe more precisely.

2971
02:06:50,079 --> 02:06:54,400
The spacetime is homogeneous,

2972
02:06:52,639 --> 02:06:58,400
meaning it looks the same at every

2973
02:06:54,400 --> 02:07:01,119
point. There is no preferred location,

2974
02:06:58,400 --> 02:07:02,719
but it is not isotropic.

2975
02:07:01,119 --> 02:07:05,520
It does not look the same in all

2976
02:07:02,719 --> 02:07:08,639
directions from a given point. The

2977
02:07:05,520 --> 02:07:11,119
rotation breaks directional symmetry.

2978
02:07:08,639 --> 02:07:14,960
Every observer sees a preferred axis

2979
02:07:11,119 --> 02:07:17,599
around which the universe rotates.

2980
02:07:14,960 --> 02:07:21,040
The matter content is a perfect fluid of

2981
02:07:17,599 --> 02:07:24,239
dust with uniform density. The pressure

2982
02:07:21,040 --> 02:07:26,960
is zero and the dust particles represent

2983
02:07:24,239 --> 02:07:29,040
idealized galaxies.

2984
02:07:26,960 --> 02:07:31,840
The fluid rotates with an angular

2985
02:07:29,040 --> 02:07:35,040
velocity related to the density by

2986
02:07:31,840 --> 02:07:37,520
Einstein's field equations.

2987
02:07:35,040 --> 02:07:40,159
Balancing rotation against gravitational

2988
02:07:37,520 --> 02:07:42,400
collapse, the universe maintains a

2989
02:07:40,159 --> 02:07:46,000
static configuration,

2990
02:07:42,400 --> 02:07:48,480
neither expanding nor contracting.

2991
02:07:46,000 --> 02:07:51,199
The metric describing distances and time

2992
02:07:48,480 --> 02:07:54,159
intervals has a specific mathematical

2993
02:07:51,199 --> 02:07:56,400
form discovered by Goodell. In

2994
02:07:54,159 --> 02:07:59,040
appropriate coordinates, it involves

2995
02:07:56,400 --> 02:08:01,360
hyperbolic functions and exhibits

2996
02:07:59,040 --> 02:08:03,440
cylindrical symmetry around the rotation

2997
02:08:01,360 --> 02:08:05,760
axis.

2998
02:08:03,440 --> 02:08:07,840
Calculating geodessics,

2999
02:08:05,760 --> 02:08:10,800
paths that freef falling observers

3000
02:08:07,840 --> 02:08:12,320
follow, reveals the closed timelike

3001
02:08:10,800 --> 02:08:15,440
curves.

3002
02:08:12,320 --> 02:08:19,440
They require traveling a long distance,

3003
02:08:15,440 --> 02:08:21,760
not just circling around a small loop.

3004
02:08:19,440 --> 02:08:24,480
One fascinating feature is that light

3005
02:08:21,760 --> 02:08:26,079
rays in Goodell's universe also behave

3006
02:08:24,480 --> 02:08:28,239
strangely.

3007
02:08:26,079 --> 02:08:31,280
A flash of light emitted from a point

3008
02:08:28,239 --> 02:08:34,159
will spread out. But due to the rotation

3009
02:08:31,280 --> 02:08:36,320
and curvature, the light rays eventually

3010
02:08:34,159 --> 02:08:38,320
recon converge at a later point on the

3011
02:08:36,320 --> 02:08:40,480
rotation axis.

3012
02:08:38,320 --> 02:08:44,880
This creates a kind of focusing effect

3013
02:08:40,480 --> 02:08:47,040
unlike anything in ordinary cosmologies.

3014
02:08:44,880 --> 02:08:49,040
Goodell also investigated whether his

3015
02:08:47,040 --> 02:08:53,360
universe could represent a realistic

3016
02:08:49,040 --> 02:08:55,440
cosmological model if modified slightly.

3017
02:08:53,360 --> 02:08:58,320
Perhaps a rotating universe with

3018
02:08:55,440 --> 02:09:01,760
expansion could match observations while

3019
02:08:58,320 --> 02:09:03,520
retaining interesting causal properties.

3020
02:09:01,760 --> 02:09:05,199
But all such attempts ran into

3021
02:09:03,520 --> 02:09:07,440
difficulties.

3022
02:09:05,199 --> 02:09:10,400
Rotation strong enough to produce closed

3023
02:09:07,440 --> 02:09:12,719
curves is incompatible with the observed

3024
02:09:10,400 --> 02:09:15,599
large-scale isotropy of the cosmic

3025
02:09:12,719 --> 02:09:18,239
microwave background.

3026
02:09:15,599 --> 02:09:20,639
Modern cosmology has placed increasingly

3027
02:09:18,239 --> 02:09:24,000
tight constraints on possible rotation

3028
02:09:20,639 --> 02:09:27,360
of the universe. Any rotation must be

3029
02:09:24,000 --> 02:09:30,719
extremely slow, far too slow to generate

3030
02:09:27,360 --> 02:09:32,800
closed timelike curves. So Goodell's

3031
02:09:30,719 --> 02:09:34,560
exact solution does not describe

3032
02:09:32,800 --> 02:09:36,480
reality.

3033
02:09:34,560 --> 02:09:38,719
But the conceptual issues it raised

3034
02:09:36,480 --> 02:09:40,800
remain relevant.

3035
02:09:38,719 --> 02:09:44,239
One issue concerns the relationship

3036
02:09:40,800 --> 02:09:46,480
between mathematics and physics.

3037
02:09:44,239 --> 02:09:48,880
General relativity is a mathematical

3038
02:09:46,480 --> 02:09:50,639
theory expressed through differential

3039
02:09:48,880 --> 02:09:52,560
geometry.

3040
02:09:50,639 --> 02:09:54,239
It makes predictions by solving

3041
02:09:52,560 --> 02:09:57,119
equations.

3042
02:09:54,239 --> 02:10:00,560
But the equations have many solutions,

3043
02:09:57,119 --> 02:10:02,639
most physically unrealistic.

3044
02:10:00,560 --> 02:10:04,239
Which solutions represent possible

3045
02:10:02,639 --> 02:10:08,079
universes?

3046
02:10:04,239 --> 02:10:10,320
Which are mere mathematical artifacts?

3047
02:10:08,079 --> 02:10:13,040
Goodell's universe is an exact solution

3048
02:10:10,320 --> 02:10:16,320
to Einstein's equations, not an

3049
02:10:13,040 --> 02:10:18,560
approximation or limiting case.

3050
02:10:16,320 --> 02:10:20,639
Mathematically, it is on equal footing

3051
02:10:18,560 --> 02:10:23,280
with the Freriedman, Roberts, and Walker

3052
02:10:20,639 --> 02:10:25,199
expanding universes that describe our

3053
02:10:23,280 --> 02:10:27,760
cosmos.

3054
02:10:25,199 --> 02:10:30,000
Yet, physically, it seems bizarre and

3055
02:10:27,760 --> 02:10:32,400
unrealistic.

3056
02:10:30,000 --> 02:10:35,040
What justifies distinguishing physically

3057
02:10:32,400 --> 02:10:37,599
reasonable solutions from unreasonable

3058
02:10:35,040 --> 02:10:40,079
ones?

3059
02:10:37,599 --> 02:10:43,679
One answer is initial conditions and

3060
02:10:40,079 --> 02:10:46,239
boundary conditions. Our universe began

3061
02:10:43,679 --> 02:10:48,159
in a big bang with specific initial

3062
02:10:46,239 --> 02:10:50,400
conditions.

3063
02:10:48,159 --> 02:10:53,119
Only solutions compatible with those

3064
02:10:50,400 --> 02:10:55,360
conditions are relevant.

3065
02:10:53,119 --> 02:10:58,159
Goodell's universe has different initial

3066
02:10:55,360 --> 02:11:00,960
conditions. It is static rather than

3067
02:10:58,159 --> 02:11:02,800
expanding, rotating rather than

3068
02:11:00,960 --> 02:11:04,800
isotropic.

3069
02:11:02,800 --> 02:11:06,719
So it is simply not the universe we

3070
02:11:04,800 --> 02:11:09,760
inhabit.

3071
02:11:06,719 --> 02:11:11,840
But Goodell would have resisted this.

3072
02:11:09,760 --> 02:11:14,880
He thought that if Einstein's equations

3073
02:11:11,840 --> 02:11:18,480
allow a type of spacetime, that type is

3074
02:11:14,880 --> 02:11:20,320
physically possible in a deep sense.

3075
02:11:18,480 --> 02:11:22,480
The equations are supposed to capture

3076
02:11:20,320 --> 02:11:24,079
the laws of gravity and space-time

3077
02:11:22,480 --> 02:11:26,400
structure.

3078
02:11:24,079 --> 02:11:28,639
If closed timelike curves are consistent

3079
02:11:26,400 --> 02:11:30,400
with those laws, then they reveal

3080
