3375
02:24:47,600 --> 02:24:52,560
generally.

3376
02:24:49,600 --> 02:24:55,040
He called his philosophy idealistic

3377
02:24:52,560 --> 02:24:57,040
yet he was a realist about mathematics

3378
02:24:55,040 --> 02:25:00,080
and physics.

3379
02:24:57,040 --> 02:25:02,399
How does this fit together?

3380
02:25:00,080 --> 02:25:06,080
The key is distinguishing different

3381
02:25:02,399 --> 02:25:09,280
forms of idealism.

3382
02:25:06,080 --> 02:25:13,280
Metaphysical idealism says reality is

3383
02:25:09,280 --> 02:25:16,000
fundamentally mental or spiritual.

3384
02:25:13,280 --> 02:25:20,479
Berkeley's idealism, for instance, holds

3385
02:25:16,000 --> 02:25:23,200
that only minds and their ideas exist.

3386
02:25:20,479 --> 02:25:25,680
Girdle rejected this.

3387
02:25:23,200 --> 02:25:29,040
He believed in an objective reality

3388
02:25:25,680 --> 02:25:31,760
independent of minds, including abstract

3389
02:25:29,040 --> 02:25:34,640
mathematical objects and physical

3390
02:25:31,760 --> 02:25:38,240
spaceime.

3391
02:25:34,640 --> 02:25:41,439
Epistemological idealism says we cannot

3392
02:25:38,240 --> 02:25:43,359
know things as they are in themselves

3393
02:25:41,439 --> 02:25:46,640
only as they appear through our

3394
02:25:43,359 --> 02:25:49,600
conceptual frameworks.

3395
02:25:46,640 --> 02:25:51,920
Kant's transcendental idealism is partly

3396
02:25:49,600 --> 02:25:54,399
