02:36:28,399 --> 02:36:34,319
well as in our minds. This argument

3634
02:36:31,040 --> 02:36:36,479
struck many as too clever to be sound.

3635
02:36:34,319 --> 02:36:39,040
How can you prove something exists just

3636
02:36:36,479 --> 02:36:41,600
by analyzing concepts?

3637
02:36:39,040 --> 02:36:43,920
Existence is not a property like wisdom

3638
02:36:41,600 --> 02:36:45,520
or power that you can build into a

3639
02:36:43,920 --> 02:36:48,800
definition.

3640
02:36:45,520 --> 02:36:51,359
Critics from Anelm's contemporary Ganilo

3641
02:36:48,800 --> 02:36:53,840
to Kant centuries later rejected

3642
02:36:51,359 --> 02:36:55,760
onlogical arguments as sophistical

3643
02:36:53,840 --> 02:36:57,760
tricks.

3644
02:36:55,760 --> 02:36:59,600
But the arguments kept reappearing in

3645
02:36:57,760 --> 02:37:02,399
new forms.

3646
02:36:59,600 --> 02:37:05,359
Daycart argued that existence belongs to

3647
02:37:02,399 --> 02:37:08,319
God's essence just as three angles

3648
02:37:05,359 --> 02:37:10,479
belong to a triangle's essence.

3649
02:37:08,319 --> 02:37:13,120
You cannot coherently conceive of God

3650
02:37:10,479 --> 02:37:15,040
without existence any more than you can

3651
02:37:13,120 --> 02:37:17,439
conceive a triangle without three

3652
02:37:15,040 --> 02:37:19,680
angles.

3653
02:37:17,439 --> 02:37:22,800
Linenets refined this by noting that the

3654
02:37:19,680 --> 02:37:26,560
argument only works if God is possible.

3655
02:37:22,800 --> 02:37:28,960
if the concept of God is coherent.

3656
02:37:26,560 --> 02:37:31,760
So, Linets attempted to prove that God's

3657
02:37:28,960 --> 02:37:34,240
existence is possible, which together

3658
02:37:31,760 --> 02:37:38,399
with the Cartisian argument would yield

3659
02:37:34,240 --> 02:37:40,720
that God necessarily exists.

3660
02:37:38,399 --> 02:37:43,439
Girdle studied Linets's version

3661
02:37:40,720 --> 02:37:47,600
intensively and developed his own proof

3662
02:37:43,439 --> 02:37:50,960
building on it. He used modal logic, the

3663
02:37:47,600 --> 02:37:53,200
logic of necessity and possibility. And

3664
02:37:50,960 --> 02:37:57,040
he worked with the concept of positive

3665
02:37:53,200 --> 02:37:59,840
properties rather than perfections.

3666
02:37:57,040 --> 02:38:02,399
The proof is technical involving axioms

3667
02:37:59,840 --> 02:38:05,280
and definitions from which conclusions

3668
02:38:02,399 --> 02:38:07,520
are derived rigorously.

3669
02:38:05,280 --> 02:38:10,000
Let me explain it step by step

3670
02:38:07,520 --> 02:38:13,200
translating the formal logic into

3671
02:38:10,000 --> 02:38:15,520
philosophical language.

3672
02:38:13,200 --> 02:38:18,479
Girdle starts with the concept of a

3673
02:38:15,520 --> 02:38:21,359
positive property. He does not define

3674
02:38:18,479 --> 02:38:24,399
what makes a property positive, treating

3675
02:38:21,359 --> 02:38:26,960
it as a primitive notion.

3676
02:38:24,399 --> 02:38:29,840
Intuitively, positive properties are

3677
02:38:26,960 --> 02:38:33,359
those that enhance or perfect whatever

3678
02:38:29,840 --> 02:38:36,640
has them. Being omnisient, being

3679
02:38:33,359 --> 02:38:40,080
omnipotent, being perfectly good. These

3680
02:38:36,640 --> 02:38:43,200
are positive. their negations being

3681
02:38:40,080 --> 02:38:45,760
ignorant, being powerless, being evil

3682
02:38:43,200 --> 02:38:48,399
are negative.

3683
02:38:45,760 --> 02:38:51,840
Axiom one says that if a property is

3684
02:38:48,399 --> 02:38:54,399
positive and that property necessarily

3685
02:38:51,840 --> 02:38:57,840
implies another property, then the

3686
02:38:54,399 --> 02:39:00,880
second property is also positive.

3687
02:38:57,840 --> 02:39:03,280
Positiveness is closed under necessary

3688
02:39:00,880 --> 02:39:06,399
implication.

3689
02:39:03,280 --> 02:39:08,800
If being omnisient is positive and

3690
02:39:06,399 --> 02:39:11,760
omniscience implies knowledge, then

3691
02:39:08,800 --> 02:39:14,720
knowledge is positive.

3692
02:39:11,760 --> 02:39:17,600
Axiom 2 says that for any property

3693
02:39:14,720 --> 02:39:19,920
either it or its negation is positive

3694
02:39:17,600 --> 02:39:22,640
but not both.

3695
02:39:19,920 --> 02:39:26,800
Every property is either positive or

3696
02:39:22,640 --> 02:39:29,680
negative. There is no neutral ground.

3697
02:39:26,800 --> 02:39:33,120
From these axioms, Girdle proves theorem

3698
02:39:29,680 --> 02:39:35,760
one. If a property is positive, then it

3699
02:39:33,120 --> 02:39:37,680
is possibly instantiated.

3700
02:39:35,760 --> 02:39:39,920
There could be something with that

3701
02:39:37,680 --> 02:39:42,800
property.

3702
02:39:39,920 --> 02:39:45,920
The proof works by contradiction.

3703
02:39:42,800 --> 02:39:49,040
If a positive property were impossible,

3704
02:39:45,920 --> 02:39:52,000
it would vacuously imply every property,

3705
02:39:49,040 --> 02:39:53,840
including negative properties.

3706
02:39:52,000 --> 02:39:57,680
But then negative properties would be

3707
02:39:53,840 --> 02:40:02,479
positive, violating axiom 2.

3708
02:39:57,680 --> 02:40:06,000
So positive properties must be possible.

3709
02:40:02,479 --> 02:40:08,640
Now Girdle defines God. A being is

3710
02:40:06,000 --> 02:40:10,319
godlike if it has every positive

3711
02:40:08,640 --> 02:40:13,680
property.

3712
02:40:10,319 --> 02:40:17,600
This is definition one. God is not

3713
02:40:13,680 --> 02:40:20,800
defined as a creator or judge or person

3714
02:40:17,600 --> 02:40:23,600
but as the instantiation of all positive

3715
02:40:20,800 --> 02:40:26,479
properties.

3716
02:40:23,600 --> 02:40:29,680
Axiom 3 says that being godlike is

3717
02:40:26,479 --> 02:40:32,720
itself a positive property.

3718
02:40:29,680 --> 02:40:34,479
This is a substantial assumption. It

3719
02:40:32,720 --> 02:40:36,720
claims that having all positive

3720
02:40:34,479 --> 02:40:38,720
properties is better than having only

3721
02:40:36,720 --> 02:40:41,680
some.

3722
02:40:38,720 --> 02:40:45,200
From axiom 3 and theorem 1, girdle

3723
02:40:41,680 --> 02:40:48,560
derives theorem 2. It is possible that

3724
02:40:45,200 --> 02:40:50,560
God exists. There could be a godlike

3725
02:40:48,560 --> 02:40:53,120
being.

3726
02:40:50,560 --> 02:40:56,160
This follows because being godlike is

3727
02:40:53,120 --> 02:40:59,800
positive and positive properties are

3728
02:40:56,160 --> 02:40:59,800
possibly instantiated.

3729
02:40:59,840 --> 02:41:05,600
So far the proof establishes only that

3730
02:41:02,399 --> 02:41:08,479
God's existence is possible, not that

3731
02:41:05,600 --> 02:41:11,359
God actually exists.

3732
02:41:08,479 --> 02:41:13,200
The next stage moves from possibility to

3733
02:41:11,359 --> 02:41:15,520
necessity.

3734
02:41:13,200 --> 02:41:17,120
Girdle introduces the concept of

3735
02:41:15,520 --> 02:41:19,359
essence.

3736
02:41:17,120 --> 02:41:22,160
A property is the essence of an

3737
02:41:19,359 --> 02:41:25,280
individual if that individual has the

3738
02:41:22,160 --> 02:41:27,359
property and the property necessarily

3739
02:41:25,280 --> 02:41:30,080
implies every other property the

3740
02:41:27,359 --> 02:41:32,960
individual has.

3741
02:41:30,080 --> 02:41:36,160
In essence captures everything essential

3742
02:41:32,960 --> 02:41:39,520
about what something is.

3743
02:41:36,160 --> 02:41:42,640
He then proves theorem three. If a being

3744
02:41:39,520 --> 02:41:45,840
is godlike, then being godlike is its

3745
02:41:42,640 --> 02:41:48,720
essence. This means God's nature is

3746
02:41:45,840 --> 02:41:50,960
captured entirely by having all positive

3747
02:41:48,720 --> 02:41:53,680
properties.

3748
02:41:50,960 --> 02:41:57,280
Nothing about God is accidental or

3749
02:41:53,680 --> 02:42:01,040
contingent beyond this.

3750
02:41:57,280 --> 02:42:03,520
Now comes axiom 4. If a property is

3751
02:42:01,040 --> 02:42:05,280
positive, then it is necessarily

3752
02:42:03,520 --> 02:42:07,439
positive.

3753
02:42:05,280 --> 02:42:09,600
Positiveness does not vary across

3754
02:42:07,439 --> 02:42:12,319
possible worlds.

3755
02:42:09,600 --> 02:42:15,520
What is positive is positive in all

3756
02:42:12,319 --> 02:42:19,200
possible circumstances.

3757
02:42:15,520 --> 02:42:22,560
Girdle defines necessary existence.

3758
02:42:19,200 --> 02:42:24,960
An individual necessarily exists if

3759
02:42:22,560 --> 02:42:28,800
every essence of that individual is

3760
02:42:24,960 --> 02:42:31,520
necessarily instantiated.

3761
02:42:28,800 --> 02:42:35,200
Necessary existence means existing in

3762
02:42:31,520 --> 02:42:37,359
all possible worlds, not just the actual

3763
02:42:35,200 --> 02:42:40,560
world.

3764
02:42:37,359 --> 02:42:43,439
Axiom 5 says that necessary existence is

3765
02:42:40,560 --> 02:42:46,800
a positive property.

3766
02:42:43,439 --> 02:42:49,439
This is the most controversial axiom.

3767
02:42:46,800 --> 02:42:52,800
It claims that existing necessarily is

3768
02:42:49,439 --> 02:42:56,399
better than existing contingently.

3769
02:42:52,800 --> 02:43:01,560
A being that could fail to exist is less

3770
02:42:56,399 --> 02:43:01,560
perfect than one that must exist.

3771
02:43:02,560 --> 02:43:07,600
From axiom 5 and the earlier results,

3772
02:43:05,200 --> 02:43:10,319
Goodell proves theorem 4. God

3773
02:43:07,600 --> 02:43:13,359
necessarily exists. The argument is

3774
02:43:10,319 --> 02:43:16,720
roughly this. Being godlike is an

3775
02:43:13,359 --> 02:43:19,520
essence of God. Necessary existence is a

3776
02:43:16,720 --> 02:43:22,000
positive property. Since God has all

3777
02:43:19,520 --> 02:43:25,120
positive properties, God has necessary

3778
02:43:22,000 --> 02:43:27,439
existence. Therefore, God's essence is

3779
02:43:25,120 --> 02:43:29,760
necessarily instantiated.

3780
02:43:27,439 --> 02:43:32,640
Therefore, God exists in all possible

3781
02:43:29,760 --> 02:43:35,280
worlds, including the actual world. This

3782
02:43:32,640 --> 02:43:37,359
is a valid logical argument. If you

3783
02:43:35,280 --> 02:43:39,680
accept the axioms and definitions, the

3784
02:43:37,359 --> 02:43:42,240
conclusion follows. Computer

3785
02:43:39,680 --> 02:43:44,800
verification has confirmed this. The

3786
02:43:42,240 --> 02:43:47,760
proof is technically correct. But does

3787
02:43:44,800 --> 02:43:49,760
it establish that God exists?

3788
02:43:47,760 --> 02:43:52,319
Nearly everyone who examines the proof

3789
02:43:49,760 --> 02:43:54,720
questions the axioms. Why should we

3790
02:43:52,319 --> 02:43:56,720
believe axiom 2 that every property is

3791
02:43:54,720 --> 02:43:59,359
either positive or negative with no

3792
02:43:56,720 --> 02:44:02,240
neutral ground? Why should we believe

3793
02:43:59,359 --> 02:44:04,960
axiom 5 that necessary existence is

3794
02:44:02,240 --> 02:44:07,840
positive? These assumptions are not

3795
02:44:04,960 --> 02:44:11,120
self-evident. They require justification

3796
02:44:07,840 --> 02:44:13,279
that Goodell did not provide.

3797
02:44:11,120 --> 02:44:16,319
The most serious objection concerns

3798
02:44:13,279 --> 02:44:18,560
modal collapse. Jordan Howard Soil

3799
02:44:16,319 --> 02:44:21,040
proved that Goodell's axioms imply that

3800
02:44:18,560 --> 02:44:23,439
if any proposition is true, it is

3801
02:44:21,040 --> 02:44:25,680
necessarily true. There are no

3802
02:44:23,439 --> 02:44:28,000
contingent truths. Everything that

3803
02:44:25,680 --> 02:44:30,160
happens must happen.

3804
02:44:28,000 --> 02:44:33,359
This is an absurd consequence that most

3805
02:44:30,160 --> 02:44:35,359
philosophers reject. If Goodell's axioms

3806
02:44:33,359 --> 02:44:38,319
lead to modal collapse, they must be

3807
02:44:35,359 --> 02:44:40,240
false. Goodell was aware of potential

3808
02:44:38,319 --> 02:44:42,319
problems but did not address modal

3809
02:44:40,240 --> 02:44:44,000
collapse explicitly.

3810
02:44:42,319 --> 02:44:46,319
Some defenders of the proof have

3811
02:44:44,000 --> 02:44:48,880
modified the axioms to avoid collapse

3812
02:44:46,319 --> 02:44:50,880
while retaining the conclusion.

3813
02:44:48,880 --> 02:44:53,600
Others argue that modal collapse is not

3814
02:44:50,880 --> 02:44:55,600
as problematic as it seems, but most

3815
02:44:53,600 --> 02:44:58,160
philosophers see it as a decisive

3816
02:44:55,600 --> 02:45:00,479
reputation. Another

3817
02:44:58,160 --> 02:45:03,120
objection raised by Graham Oppy and

3818
02:45:00,479 --> 02:45:06,000
others is that the axioms prove too

3819
02:45:03,120 --> 02:45:07,920
much. If Goodell's reasoning works,

3820
02:45:06,000 --> 02:45:09,920
similar arguments could establish the

3821
02:45:07,920 --> 02:45:13,760
necessary existence of all sorts of

3822
02:45:09,920 --> 02:45:16,399
entities, a maximally evil being, an

3823
02:45:13,760 --> 02:45:19,439
almost god lacking one property, or

3824
02:45:16,399 --> 02:45:21,600
other bizarre objects. The proof seems

3825
02:45:19,439 --> 02:45:25,040
to show not that God exists, but that

3826
02:45:21,600 --> 02:45:26,640
the axioms are defective.

3827
02:45:25,040 --> 02:45:30,000
There is also the question of what the

3828
02:45:26,640 --> 02:45:31,920
proof establishes even if valid. The

3829
02:45:30,000 --> 02:45:34,080
godlike being in Goodell's proof is

3830
02:45:31,920 --> 02:45:36,479
defined purely by having all positive

3831
02:45:34,080 --> 02:45:39,359
properties. But this seems distant from

3832
02:45:36,479 --> 02:45:42,479
the god of religious tradition. Does the

3833
02:45:39,359 --> 02:45:45,680
godlike being care about humans? Does it

3834
02:45:42,479 --> 02:45:48,319
answer prayers, perform miracles, judge

3835
02:45:45,680 --> 02:45:50,080
the living and the dead? None of this

3836
02:45:48,319 --> 02:45:51,840
follows from having all positive

3837
02:45:50,080 --> 02:45:53,760
properties.

3838
02:45:51,840 --> 02:45:56,560
Goodell's god might be an impersonal

3839
02:45:53,760 --> 02:45:59,439
principle or an abstract perfection

3840
02:45:56,560 --> 02:46:02,319
rather than a personal deity. Goodell

3841
02:45:59,439 --> 02:46:03,840
himself recognized this gap. He told

3842
02:46:02,319 --> 02:46:06,160
Morgan Stern that the proof was a

3843
02:46:03,840 --> 02:46:07,840
logical exercise, not a religious

3844
02:46:06,160 --> 02:46:09,439
argument.

3845
02:46:07,840 --> 02:46:11,680
Whether the god-like being whose

3846
02:46:09,439 --> 02:46:14,640
existence is proven corresponds to the

3847
02:46:11,680 --> 02:46:16,800
god of Christianity or Judaism or Islam

3848
02:46:14,640 --> 02:46:18,560
is a further question.

3849
02:46:16,800 --> 02:46:20,800
The proof shows at most that something

3850
02:46:18,560 --> 02:46:22,800
with maximal perfections exists

3851
02:46:20,800 --> 02:46:24,319
necessarily.

3852
02:46:22,800 --> 02:46:26,319
Identifying this with the god of

3853
02:46:24,319 --> 02:46:27,920
religious belief requires additional

3854
02:46:26,319 --> 02:46:31,359
argument.

3855
02:46:27,920 --> 02:46:33,200
Why then did Goodell work on the proof?

3856
02:46:31,359 --> 02:46:34,720
Several motivations seem to have

3857
02:46:33,200 --> 02:46:38,160
converged.

3858
02:46:34,720 --> 02:46:39,600
First, intellectual curiosity.

3859
02:46:38,160 --> 02:46:42,560
Ontological arguments are

3860
02:46:39,600 --> 02:46:44,560
philosophically fascinating puzzles.

3861
02:46:42,560 --> 02:46:46,479
Showing that rigorous modal logic could

3862
02:46:44,560 --> 02:46:49,359
formalize and extend them was an

3863
02:46:46,479 --> 02:46:52,000
achievement in itself.

3864
02:46:49,359 --> 02:46:54,160
Second, his rationalism.

3865
02:46:52,000 --> 02:46:57,680
Goodell believed pure reason could reach

3866
02:46:54,160 --> 02:47:00,240
metaphysical truths. An onlogical proof,

3867
02:46:57,680 --> 02:47:02,640
if successful, would vindicate this

3868
02:47:00,240 --> 02:47:05,840
conviction.

3869
02:47:02,640 --> 02:47:07,760
Third, his theological interests.

3870
02:47:05,840 --> 02:47:10,319
Though he kept them private, Goodell

3871
02:47:07,760 --> 02:47:12,399
held religious beliefs.

3872
02:47:10,319 --> 02:47:15,040
Proving God's existence through logic

3873
02:47:12,399 --> 02:47:16,800
would support those beliefs.

3874
02:47:15,040 --> 02:47:19,920
But Goodell also seems to have had

3875
02:47:16,800 --> 02:47:22,720
doubts. He refined the proof repeatedly

3876
02:47:19,920 --> 02:47:24,720
over decades, suggesting he found flaws

3877
02:47:22,720 --> 02:47:27,040
or limitations.

3878
02:47:24,720 --> 02:47:29,359
He never published it, suggesting he was

3879
02:47:27,040 --> 02:47:30,880
not fully satisfied.

3880
02:47:29,359 --> 02:47:33,120
And his statement to Morgan Stern

3881
02:47:30,880 --> 02:47:35,120
reveals ambivalence about how the proof

3882
02:47:33,120 --> 02:47:37,040
should be understood.

3883
02:47:35,120 --> 02:47:38,880
One interpretation is that Goodell saw

3884
02:47:37,040 --> 02:47:41,040
the proof as showing what follows from

3885
02:47:38,880 --> 02:47:43,120
certain assumptions about positiveness

3886
02:47:41,040 --> 02:47:44,720
and perfection.

3887
02:47:43,120 --> 02:47:47,439
If you grant that perfections are

3888
02:47:44,720 --> 02:47:49,520
positive, that God has all perfections

3889
02:47:47,439 --> 02:47:53,920
and that necessary existence is a

3890
02:47:49,520 --> 02:47:56,000
perfection, then God exists necessarily.

3891
02:47:53,920 --> 02:47:57,680
This conditional claim is what the logic

3892
02:47:56,000 --> 02:48:00,160
establishes.

3893
02:47:57,680 --> 02:48:02,560
Whether the antecedent is true requires

3894
02:48:00,160 --> 02:48:04,160
philosophical argument beyond the formal

3895
02:48:02,560 --> 02:48:06,000
proof.

3896
02:48:04,160 --> 02:48:08,240
This would make the ontological argument

3897
02:48:06,000 --> 02:48:10,399
a tool for clarifying concepts rather

3898
02:48:08,240 --> 02:48:12,319
than a demonstration.

3899
02:48:10,399 --> 02:48:14,319
It shows what commitments are entailed

3900
02:48:12,319 --> 02:48:17,279
by believing in a maximally perfect

3901
02:48:14,319 --> 02:48:19,920
being. It reveals the structure of the

3902
02:48:17,279 --> 02:48:22,240
concept of God, but it does not prove

3903
02:48:19,920 --> 02:48:24,720
God exists unless you already accept the

3904
02:48:22,240 --> 02:48:26,640
axioms.

3905
02:48:24,720 --> 02:48:29,200
Contemporary work on the ontological

3906
02:48:26,640 --> 02:48:31,439
argument has taken various directions.

3907
02:48:29,200 --> 02:48:33,120
Some philosophers use modal logic to

3908
02:48:31,439 --> 02:48:36,000
explore different versions of the

3909
02:48:33,120 --> 02:48:38,399
